## Overall Summary  

2025 was normal-to-dry across the MSEP watershed. In terms of the annual total precipitation received, about 1/3 of the subbasins were within 5% of the 30-year average total. The others ranged about 10-20% lower for their annual totals. The subbasins that were driest were generally in the southern portions of the watershed, whereas the more northern subbasins were closer to the long-term average. See @fig-mapPrcpTotalAndAnomPct and @fig-precipPctDiff in particular for details. 

In terms of monthly totals, May was a little bit wet, particularly in the middle portion of the watershed, and the dry months were September and November. See @fig-mapPrcpMonthlyAnoms.

For a summary table of annual and monthly totals, normals, and % difference from normal, see @tbl-prcpAnoms.


