### Monthly Precipitation  

Monthly data are from the PRISM Group at Oregon State University, https://prism.oregonstate.edu and were accessed 29 July 2026. They are again averaged to HUC8. Monthly normals are also from the PRISM group, and were compiled in the [`msepBaselineData`](https://github.com/CMEP-MS/msepBaselineData) R package.


::: {.cell}

:::



::: {.cell}

:::



::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Map of monthly precipitation totals (inches), averaged to the HUC-8 (subbasin) level.](precipitation_files/figure-pdf/fig-mapPrcpMonthlyTotals-1.pdf){#fig-mapPrcpMonthlyTotals}
:::
:::


May seems to have been the wettest month in 2025, and that's not really typical - actually in the climate normals (see them [here](https://msepcharacterization.netlify.app/precipitation#monthly-totals-30-year-normal)), the color scale only goes up to 8.5 inches per month, and May 2025 exceeded that.  

